---
/**
 * PARENTS' FEEDBACK — /parents-feedback/
 *
 * ⚠ THE URL IS /parents-feedback/, NOT UNDER /academics/parent-partnership/.
 * It is linked from the Parent Partnership mega-menu all the same — the one
 * entry in that group whose path sits outside the section, on the client's
 * instruction. Without that nav entry the page would be an orphan.
 *
 * ⚠⚠ `crumbs` EXCLUDES THE CURRENT PAGE. PageHero appends it from `title` and
 * marks it aria-current. Passing "Parents' Feedback" in the array prints it
 * twice.
 *
 * ⚠ STOCK PageHero, CENTRED. No left-aligned split hero. An earlier pass
 * matched a left-aligned comp, which needed an `align` prop on PageHero plus
 * page-level overrides reaching into a shared component's scoped styles. Both
 * were reverted, and PageHero is untouched.
 *
 * ⚠⚠ THE BANNER IS NOT THE ONE THE BRIEF NAMES, BECAUSE THAT FILE DOES NOT
 * EXIST. The brief asks for src/assets/photos/campus-entrance-wall.jpg — the
 * drive with the school's name carved into the brick wall. That path is not in
 * the repository and never has been (checked against git history, not just the
 * working tree), and the only photograph of that wall in the project is
 * alumni-meets/…/06-entrance-before-the-meet.jpg, which is dressed for an
 * alumni meet: red carpet, house banners and an "Alumni Meet 2026" standee. A
 * parents' feedback page is the wrong place for it, and its alt text could not
 * honestly be the one the brief supplies.
 *
 * So this keeps the Parents' Forum photograph, which is at least about parents.
 * When the real file is added, this route needs exactly two lines changed — the
 * import and the alt — and the brief's alt text is recorded here ready for it:
 *
 *   "The drive inside Sunbeam School Ballia at Agarsanda, the school's name
 *    carved into the brick wall with palms and potted plants along it."
 *
 * ⚠ TITLE AND CRUMBS ARE PASSED EXPLICITLY. Most static routes take their SEO
 * from a CMS page-meta row keyed on the path; this route has no such row yet.
 * Seed one and these props can come out.
 *
 * The panel's padding-block is an inline style — a scoped rule can skew against
 * its build hash and reopen the white band above the footer.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import ParentsFeedbackPage from '../components/academics/partnership/ParentsFeedbackPage.astro';

import banner from '../assets/parents forum/parents forum (5).jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Parents’ Feedback — Sunbeam School Ballia"
  description="How parents take part at Sunbeam School Ballia — the Parents’ Forum, the Child Parent Teacher Dialogue, the orientation programmes, and a form for sending the school your own feedback."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Parents’ Feedback"
    standfirst="Voices from our school community"
    crumbs={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Parent Partnership', href: '/academics/parent-partnership/' },
    ]}
    src={banner}
    alt="Parents seated at the Parents’ Forum at Sunbeam School Ballia."
    position="46% 58%"
  />

  <div class="u-page-panel" style="padding-block: 0;">
    <ParentsFeedbackPage />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
